# Example dotenv file for paperless-tax-export. It holds placeholders only.
#
# Copy it OUTSIDE this repository, remove the "# " from the lines you need and make it
# readable only by you:
#
#   cp .env.example /path/to/paperless.env && chmod 600 /path/to/paperless.env
#   uv run paperless-tax-export audit --env-file /path/to/paperless.env
#
# Every line is commented out on purpose. A variable that is set but blank is an error
# (exit 2) and does not fall through to the default, so leave a line commented until it
# has a value. A real environment variable wins over an entry here. A .env in the working
# directory is never loaded: the file is read only when you name it with --env-file or
# PAPERLESS_ENV_FILE.
#
# The file is parsed by python-dotenv, not by compose: write values without $, quotes or #.

# Paperless-ngx
# The view-only API token (plain hex). Never commit a real token.
# PAPERLESS_TOKEN=
# Base URL of the instance, http:// or https:// (default http://localhost:8000).
# PAPERLESS_BASE_URL=https://paperless.example.com

# Estimate
# Marginal tax rate as a decimal fraction from 0 to 1, for example 0.32. Optional: without
# it estimate.csv has no tax_saving row.
# TAX_MARGINAL_RATE=

# Work-from-home scenarios in estimate.csv. All optional; a missing value leaves that row
# as "not computed".
# Hours worked from home in the year (fixed-rate scenario).
# WFH_HOURS=
# Fixed rate in AUD per hour. There is no default: you supply it.
# WFH_RATE_PER_HOUR=
# Work-use share of the internet and phone bills, as a percentage from 0 to 100 (50 is half).
# WFH_INTERNET_PCT=
# WFH_PHONE_PCT=
# Your own appliance-based energy figure in AUD.
# WFH_ENERGY_AMOUNT=
